card.statement:
Let $D$ be a ring, and $\sigma=(\sigma_1, \ldots, \sigma_n)$ an $n$-tuple of commuting automorphisms: $\sigma_i \sigma_j = \sigma_j \sigma_i$, $i$, $j=1$, \dots, $n$. Let $a=(a_1,\ldots,a_n)$ be an $n$-tuple of non-zero elements belonging to the centre of $D$, such that $\sigma_i(a_j)=a_j$ whenever $j \neq i$. The generalized Weyl algebra (GWA) $D(a, \sigma)$ of degree $n$ and base ring $D$ is generated over $D$ by $X_i^+$, $X_i^-$, $i=1$, \dots, $n$, satisfying the following relations

\begin{subequations}
\begin{gather}
X_i^+(d)= \sigma_i(d) X_i^+, \qquad  X_i^- d= \sigma_i^{-1}(d) X_i^-,\quad  d \in D,\\
[X_i^+, X_j^+]=[X_i^-,X_j^-]=[X_i^+, X_j^-]=0, \quad i\neq j,\\
X_i^- X_i^+ = a_i, \qquad X_i^+  X_i^- = \sigma_i(a_i).
\end{gather}
\end{subequations}
